# Do not delete this file, and do not "simplify" it away.
#
# Our .gitignore excludes media/ and public-data/library.json on purpose - the
# audio is the user's own, and it does not belong in a public git repo.
#
# THE VOLUME CHANGED WHAT THIS MEANS. The library and all audio now live on the
# Railway volume mounted at /data (see server/storage.js), which survives
# deploys. media/ and public-data/ in the repo are no longer what the deployed
# app reads - they are only a SEED, copied onto the volume once by
# seedFromBundleIfEmpty() when the volume has no library.json yet.
#
# So, in practice:
#
#   * First deploy onto a brand-new, empty volume - ship the seed data:
#
#       railway up --no-gitignore
#
#     (railway CLI v5.23.2 applies .gitignore rules on top of .railwayignore
#     regardless of this file, so without that flag the gitignored media/ and
#     public-data/library.json never leave your machine.)
#
#   * Every deploy after that - plain `railway up` is enough. The volume
#     already holds the library and the audio, the seed is a no-op, and
#     forgetting the flag no longer costs anything.
#
# Songs added through the app's own upload button go straight to the volume and
# were never in the repo to begin with, so they are unaffected either way.
#
# Worth one check after the first deploy onto a fresh volume:
# curl <url>/api/library (after logging in) and confirm it is not
# {"tracks":[],"playlists":[]}.
#
# This file's own listed patterns (build junk, sample fixtures) apply normally
# on top of all of the above.

node_modules
.git
.gitignore

# Local data directory - the development stand-in for the volume. Never ship it.
.localdata

# Test fixtures - generated tones, not real library content.
tools/sample

# Local-only cruft.
.env
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*
